Common Air Conditioning Problems
If your cooling system isn't operating properly, you may notice one or more of the following issues:
    • AC blowing warm air 
    • Weak or uneven airflow 
    • Frozen evaporator coils 
    • Refrigerant leaks 
    • Faulty thermostat 
    • Strange noises or vibrations 
    • Water leaking around the unit 
    • Frequent cycling 
    • High energy bills 
    • Electrical component failures 
Ignoring these warning signs can reduce system efficiency and increase repair costs over time.
